/T (Cornell Hack4Impact Endowment Manager is an open-source tool we are building in collaboration with Cornell alum David Strip to assist non-profits and smaller organizations with managing endowments through a streamlined platform. This is the project's 4th semester, and we are wrapping up development and deployment of our MVP, along with finalizing designs and completing user testing. As an internal project, we are also continuing to iterate on new ideas such as directly importing transactions from CSV files to further streamline endowment management.)
/E (Cornell Hack4Impact Endowment Manager is an open-source tool we are building in collaboration with Cornell alum David Strip to assist non-profits and smaller organizations with managing endowments through a streamlined platform. This is the project's 4th semester, and we are wrapping up development and deployment of our MVP, along with finalizing designs and completing user testing. As an internal project, we are also continuing to iterate on new ideas such as directly importing transactions from CSV files to further streamline endowment management.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 365 0 R
/T (Rethink Food is a nonprofit that partners with restaurants, kitchens, and community-based organizations \(CBOs\) to increase food security and reduce waste. Rethink Food strengthens local food ecosystems, connecting restaurant partners with CBOs and delivering measurable impact at the neighborhood level. We're building a map-based web app that visualizes the flow of meals from restaurant partners to CBOs across NYC. The tool replaces scattered Google Sheets with a Postgres backend and features a donor-friendly, interactive interface with search capabilities, filters, impact overlays, and baseline comparisons to highlight gaps.)
/E (Rethink Food is a nonprofit that partners with restaurants, kitchens, and community-based organizations \(CBOs\) to increase food security and reduce waste. Rethink Food strengthens local food ecosystems, connecting restaurant partners with CBOs and delivering measurable impact at the neighborhood level. We're building a map-based web app that visualizes the flow of meals from restaurant partners to CBOs across NYC. The tool replaces scattered Google Sheets with a Postgres backend and features a donor-friendly, interactive interface with search capabilities, filters, impact overlays, and baseline comparisons to highlight gaps.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
